    "body": "- socketserver (incompatible with Nvim's channel/server (docs))\r\n- w32\r\n- x11\r\n\r\nTarget patches (none are N/A though):\r\n\r\n- [ ] v9.1.1651\r\n- [X] 39a67920fbd8bbdd0af8435a4e0f7c1bd0c4822c\r\n- [ ] v9.1.1857\r\n- [ ] 7e585b6fa4d26a18cd7ab6d95d20d5f091ff5f28\r\n- [ ] b8c1ef5a6479b8d41bea921c602c8a982d249de0\r\n- [ ] v9.2.0512\r\n- [ ] v9.2.0600\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nThere's not enough vimhelp tags to avoid treating `has-patch` like `:version` . Have to upstream new tags or just `N/A` it.\r\nI don't want to add special-case each hunk header to that extent.\r\n\r\nInstead, I'm curious if treesitter or some parser or syntax engine can be used to analyze the diffs.\r\nIt doesn't have to compile. Just enough to reuse existing pattern files and avoid/reduce/simplify regexp.",
