            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "My statement for v9.1.1651 is based on `is_na_patch()` ; I didn't manually review the entire patch even if I exclude `wayland` feature. I also assumed `remote.txt` is technically applicable for the remaining support cli flags. I didn't treat it like `:version` (https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41018); I was expecting a feedback, not a quick merge, even if it's been N/A for years now.\r\n\r\nFrom your POV, the shared filename is just an \"inherited relic of the past\" and it's been that way in totality; updating via `vim-patch` is a bonus; Any similarities is not intended unless stated explicitly.\r\n\r\n--------\r\n\r\nStill, due to Vim's later rework (8.2.x?) on builtin/supported feature detection, technically, it can't be 100% N/A via  automation. If `wayland` is N/A in principle for `src/nvim/` (ignoring any possible code reuse from Vim's `clipmethod`), then I can blacklist some files/hunks to let `vim-patch.sh` detect the followup N/A patches from v9.1.1651 as mitigation.",
